{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00176",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.87,
      "end_seconds": 6.3,
      "duration_seconds": 5.43,
      "text": "Doctor, I've checked them in and done the preliminary measurements, I'll hand them over when you ask."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.51,
      "end_seconds": 10.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "Thank you. Right, hello, what's the problem?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 10.52,
      "end_seconds": 16.49,
      "duration_seconds": 5.97,
      "text": "I mean, doctor, I've come along because I know the history, if it helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 16.9,
      "end_seconds": 19.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "Absolutely, come and sit beside them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 20.46,
      "end_seconds": 30.24,
      "duration_seconds": 9.78,
      "text": "I wanted to get breathlessness when I lie flat looked at. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 31.39,
      "end_seconds": 33.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "Okay, how long have you had it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 34.07,
      "end_seconds": 35.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "About... well, three weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.37,
      "end_seconds": 42.5,
      "duration_seconds": 6.13,
      "text": "And the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 42.6,
      "end_seconds": 48.92,
      "duration_seconds": 6.32,
      "text": "Hmm, um, tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.45,
      "end_seconds": 53.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "I was getting to that!"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 56.71,
      "end_seconds": 59.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "Right, any swelling in both ankles as well?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.35,
      "end_seconds": 64.3,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Yeah. Five days, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 65.72,
      "end_seconds": 68.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "On a normal day, how strong is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 69.55,
      "end_seconds": 70.89,
      "duration_seconds": 1.34,
      "text": "It's severe, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "UNKNOWN",
      "start_seconds": 71.98,
      "end_seconds": 74.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "Mm, that's what happened, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.93,
      "end_seconds": 75.66,
      "duration_seconds": 0.73,
      "text": "Any fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 76.41,
      "end_seconds": 77.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.28,
      "text": "No, no fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 79.09,
      "end_seconds": 83.33,
      "duration_seconds": 4.24,
      "text": "Actually, doctor, I did notice fever. She doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.44,
      "end_seconds": 89.85,
      "duration_seconds": 5.41,
      "text": "Yeah, no, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 91.24,
      "end_seconds": 99.56,
      "duration_seconds": 8.32,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Any coughing up blood, chest pain, palpitations or calf pain at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.99,
      "end_seconds": 112.27,
      "duration_seconds": 12.28,
      "text": "No, no coughing up blood, no chest pain, no palpitations. I did have a dry cough at night at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.8,
      "end_seconds": 114.53,
      "duration_seconds": 1.73,
      "text": "Anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 115.22,
      "end_seconds": 116.6,
      "duration_seconds": 1.38,
      "text": "Nothing there, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 120.94,
      "end_seconds": 127.15,
      "duration_seconds": 6.21,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Saturation 90 percent, heart rate 92, BP is 136 over 74."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.79,
      "end_seconds": 131.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "Okay, good, thank you. How's everything else at home otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 131.46,
      "end_seconds": 137.72,
      "duration_seconds": 6.26,
      "text": "Busy. Everyone's running in different directions at the moment, you know how it is."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 138.83,
      "end_seconds": 139.84,
      "duration_seconds": 1.01,
      "text": "What about alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.19,
      "end_seconds": 145.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "I gave up drinking about three years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.13,
      "end_seconds": 149.06,
      "duration_seconds": 0.93,
      "text": "Do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 149.62,
      "end_seconds": 152.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "I smoke, yes, around five a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 153.84,
      "end_seconds": 157.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "Let me just pull up your file for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 157.79,
      "end_seconds": 158.49,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.38,
      "end_seconds": 172.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 173.6,
      "end_seconds": 177.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "Yes, I had my appendix out, about eight years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.56,
      "end_seconds": 182.69,
      "duration_seconds": 4.13,
      "text": "What medicines do you take regularly? Take your time, there's no rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 183.22,
      "end_seconds": 188.3,
      "duration_seconds": 5.08,
      "text": "I take clopidogrel, 75 milligrams, once a day for the stent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 189.41,
      "end_seconds": 193.61,
      "duration_seconds": 4.2,
      "text": "Doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 37.5 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.46,
      "end_seconds": 199.09,
      "duration_seconds": 4.63,
      "text": "Okay. Have you got the newest prescription or the box with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 199.4,
      "end_seconds": 203.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "So, not with me. I'll bring it next time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 204.53,
      "end_seconds": 212.0,
      "duration_seconds": 7.47,
      "text": "It's a... um, um, I can't remember what it's called. It's a small white one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.79,
      "end_seconds": 215.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "Right, do you remember what it's for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 216.5,
      "end_seconds": 230.39,
      "duration_seconds": 13.89,
      "text": "I mean, for my heart, I believe. My husband sets them out for me, I just take what I'm given. Uh, I was on losartan before. I stopped taking it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.8,
      "end_seconds": 233.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "Do you have any known allergies at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 234.77,
      "end_seconds": 245.8,
      "duration_seconds": 11.03,
      "text": "Hmm, there was some antibiotic, I was told I was allergic. But I couldn't tell you what it was called or what it did."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.75,
      "end_seconds": 248.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "Let me double-check something in your record."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 249.76,
      "end_seconds": 251.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "Of course, take your time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.8,
      "end_seconds": 274.95,
      "duration_seconds": 8.15,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. What about your general health, any conditions you're being treated for? Bear with me, I'm just building up the picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 275.86,
      "end_seconds": 287.58,
      "duration_seconds": 11.72,
      "text": "I've had diabetes for about a year now. I have heart disease. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't. Yes, high blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 288.23,
      "end_seconds": 289.15,
      "duration_seconds": 0.92,
      "text": "Okay. Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 290.27,
      "end_seconds": 296.16,
      "duration_seconds": 5.89,
      "text": "So, yes, heart failure. My family kept telling me to get it checked."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.56,
      "end_seconds": 321.98,
      "duration_seconds": 25.42,
      "text": "Yes, I can see the heart disease in your file as well. Right, so that's your known high blood pressure. We'll keep that in mind today. Let me explain how I'm thinking about this. When someone has symptoms like these, we first look for the common and treatable causes, and only then for the rarer ones. That's why I'm going step by step rather than ordering everything at once."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 322.9,
      "end_seconds": 324.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.79,
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 325.14,
      "end_seconds": 342.13,
      "duration_seconds": 16.99,
      "text": "Okay, so my impression from what you've said is this: It fits best with fluid overload related to the heart. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. It could also be a chest infection, so we'll keep that open."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 343.18,
      "end_seconds": 347.34,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "I've been thinking the worst, to be honest. Is it bad?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 348.65,
      "end_seconds": 366.23,
      "duration_seconds": 17.58,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with fluid overload related to the heart do well once it's treated properly. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had breathlessness when you lie flat for three weeks, and no chest pain or calf pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 367.67,
      "end_seconds": 370.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "Exactly, you know, that's what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 371.85,
      "end_seconds": 379.6,
      "duration_seconds": 7.75,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange an ECG for breathlessness. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_6",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 379.98,
      "end_seconds": 383.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "We have a slot Thursday at 2 pm, if that works."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 384.73,
      "end_seconds": 412.37,
      "duration_seconds": 27.64,
      "text": "We should do an echocardiogram for breathlessness and swelling. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. I'd like to arrange a chest X-ray for breathlessness. Keep the salt and the fluids moderate, no more than about one and a half litres a day. Weigh yourself every morning, and tell us if you put on more than two kilos in a few days. Please take the tablets with food so they don't upset your stomach."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 412.99,
      "end_seconds": 420.22,
      "duration_seconds": 7.23,
      "text": "And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 421.16,
      "end_seconds": 423.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Okay, uh, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 424.15,
      "end_seconds": 438.6,
      "duration_seconds": 14.45,
      "text": "I want you to come back or go to emergency straight away if the breathlessness gets worse or you can't lie down at all. Please come and see me in one week. Okay, summarise it for me, what's the plan from your side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 439.67,
      "end_seconds": 444.82,
      "duration_seconds": 5.15,
      "text": "So, uh, I come back in one week. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 446.26,
      "end_seconds": 449.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Okay, we're done for today. Take care."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 450.85,
      "end_seconds": 453.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "Alright, uh, thanks. Bye for now."
    }
  ]
}